            <ArticleTitle>[Measurement of peripheral venous pressure using Doppler ultrasound].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A method for determining peripheral venous pressure in the cubital vein by means of dopplerography is described. Fifty-four subjects (12 normal subjects, 19 hypertensive patients and 23 coronary patients) have been investigated. Patients with cardiovascular diseases showed somewhat increased peripheral venous pressure. The method is simple, non-invasive, it permits continuous monitoring of pressure in a major, easily-accessible vein and is not time-consuming.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
